    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d436">

                <pb facs="0534" n="446" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg446"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/951: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Cuba</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Guggenheim</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-02T18:00:00-05:00">February 2, 1933—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5. Your 8, February 2, noon. Please explain to Mr. Ferrara the background of the
                    Leticia matter as set forth in the telegram which the Secretary of State sent to
                    the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Peru on January 25, a copy of which was sent
                    to you in Department’s circular instruction of same date.<anchor n="80"
                        xml:id="d436-f1"/> Colombia is merely defending her own territory; territory
                    which has been recognized by all, including <pb facs="0535" n="447"
                        xml:id="pg447"/> Peruvian Government, as being Colombian. Department thinks
                    it important that Cuba should support action on basis of Kellogg Pact.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
